   finding run_counts_missing (info): No per-run `metrics` row from results.txt for `psms_1pct` (1 of 1 runs), `peptides` (1 of 1 runs), `protein_groups` (1 of 1 runs), `precursors` (1 of 1 runs), `ms2_scans` (1 of 1 runs). These counts were not written, which is not a count of zero. MetaMorpheus writes results.txt's per-file lines only for a search of two or more files, and this deposit has one run, so its deposit-wide rows (`scope = 'dataset'`) count that run. Each run's MS2 spectra are also counted by the QC report, in `runs.ms2_spectra` and `metrics` (`name = 'ms2'`, `source = 'qc_report.json'`), for 1 of the 1 runs. PXReprise's QC payload counts each run's share of the whole search's 1% set instead, a different number (the FDR is the whole search's, not recomputed on each file), under names of its own (`source = 'qc_payload.json'`): `psms_1pct_whole_search` for 1 of the 1 runs, `peptides_1pct_whole_search` for 1 of the 1 runs, `protein_groups_1pct_whole_search` for none of them.
